## 5. Accuracy and Correctness Analysis

The design successfully classifies the complete 5-bit input range into four age categories. Boundary conditions at ages 12, 13, 19, 20, 25 and 26 are particularly important for verifying correct range detection.

The testbench results indicate 100% correctness across the 32 tested input combinations.

## 6. Known Limitations

- The input range is restricted to 0–31 because of the 5-bit input.
- Physical FPGA output verification is separate from behavioral simulation.
- Pushbutton debouncing and synchronisation may be required for reliable hardware operation.
- Hardware testing must be completed to confirm the physical LED outputs.

## 7. Conclusion

The simulation results confirm that the Age Group Detector correctly classifies all 32 possible input combinations according to the specified four age groups. The design successfully demonstrates range detection, register-based input storage and Moore FSM operation.
